---
import LegalDocument from '../../components/LegalDocument.astro';
import { legalDates, legalUrls } from '../../lib/legal';
const { canonical, alternate } = legalUrls('en', '/terms', '/terms');
---
<LegalDocument lang="en" title="Terms of Service" metaTitle="Terms of Service | Repero AI" description="Terms governing use of Repero AI, subject to the commercial clauses still to be finalized." canonical={canonical} alternate={alternate} lastUpdated={legalDates.en} eyebrow="Terms">
  <aside class="legal-document__notice" aria-label="Publication status"><p><strong>Commercial terms are not final.</strong> The contracting identity, customer regime, payment terms, consumer information, liability terms, and post-termination arrangements require owner and legal review before payment opening. This page intentionally does not invent them.</p></aside>
  <h2>1. Scope and service</h2><p>These Terms govern access to Repero AI, a workspace intended to help users keep, organize, retrieve, and reuse AI-assisted work, including conversations, documents, sources, and generated artefacts. The public website is informational; product use takes place through the application.</p>
  <h2>2. Eligibility and account access</h2><p>You may use the service only where you can lawfully enter into these Terms and comply with applicable law. Account access may require registration and authentication. You are responsible for safeguarding your credentials and for activity carried out through your account, to the extent permitted by applicable law.</p>
  <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2><p>You must not use Repero to violate law or third-party rights; upload content you are not entitled to use; introduce malware or harmful code; attempt unauthorized access; interfere with service security; or facilitate harmful, fraudulent, or unlawful activity.</p>
  <h2>4. User content and permissions</h2><p>You remain responsible for the content you submit, including having the necessary rights, permissions, and lawful basis to upload, process, or share it. You retain your rights in that content. You grant the service operator the limited, non-exclusive rights necessary to host, store, process, index, display, retrieve, and transmit the content solely to operate and improve the requested service functionality, subject to applicable law and the Privacy Policy.</p>
  <h2>5. Repero intellectual property</h2><p>Repero’s software, interface, branding, and related materials are owned by or licensed to the final contracting entity. These Terms do not transfer ownership of those materials to users. The final contracting entity must be supplied before commercial publication.</p>
  <h2>6. AI-assisted output</h2><p>Repero uses AI systems and generative models. Output may be incomplete, incorrect, misleading, or unsuitable for a particular context. Repero does not present AI output as inherently authoritative. You must review output as appropriate before relying on it, especially for legal, financial, medical, safety-critical, professional, or other material decisions. Repero does not provide professional advice.</p>
  <h2>7. Service protection and fair use</h2><p>Repero may apply reasonable technical, security, storage, usage, or rate limits to protect the service and other users. It may investigate and address activity that creates a security, legal, or material operational risk.</p>
  <h2>8. Suspension and termination</h2><p>You may stop using the service at any time. Repero may suspend or restrict access where reasonably necessary for security, legal compliance, protection of others, or a material breach of these Terms. Notice will be provided where appropriate and practicable, except where immediate action is needed.</p>
  <h2>9. Service changes</h2><p>The service may evolve, including features, limits, and availability. Material changes should be communicated through an appropriate channel where required by law or contract.</p>
  <h2>10. Clauses pending commercial decisions</h2><p>The following are deliberately reserved for finalization before payment opening: contracting identity; B2C/B2B treatment; prices, VAT and invoices; subscription, renewal and cancellation mechanics; consumer withdrawal; refunds or credits; liability limitations; post-termination export period; and controller/processor or DPA terms for organizational customers.</p>
  <h2>11. Governing law and contact</h2><p>The governing-law, jurisdiction, consumer-protection, and contact clauses must be completed after the contracting identity and customer approach are confirmed. Mandatory consumer protections will apply where applicable.</p>
</LegalDocument>
